{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27199-what-if-the-nameless-empire-was-not-in-the-past-but-a-future-event","id":27199,"title":"What if the Nameless Empire was not in the past but a future event.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-10T08:12:30-08:00","id":27199,"title":"What if the Nameless Empire was not in the past but a future event.","content":"Okay just bare with me this is just a weird dream I had last night. What the Fall of the Nameless Empire was not an event in the past but one of in the future? Perhaps that is why it has no name because it is yet to be named, yeah I know the real reason is names have power so be rid of them. So in my dream the Arisen are a result of backwards causality of the sacrifice of the Nameless Empire creating the Arisen in the past numerous Sothic turns ago. The accumulation of Relics is actually to power this ritual bolstering the Nameless empire with items of power from around history. There was some other part of the dream I'm trying to remember, ironically I think it had to do with memory, like what if memory(or maybe it was sekhem) was something the mummies choose to gave up to quicken this cycle of events. So the Shan'iatu and or Judges are to be birthed/created in the Future with mummies that have discovered the secret turning rogue and forestalling the events by hording relics.<br /> <br /> I don't like I said it was a weird crazy dream I had a few hours ago that I'm loosing more and more detail on. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T10:08:19-08:00","id":27274,"title":"","content":"Is that not one of the theories of Atlantis from Secrets of the Ruined Temple? Were you reading that before you went to sleep <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can see the logic to it, however unlike Atlantis, Irem is pretty irrevocably tied to it's era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:32:40-08:00","id":27889,"title":"","content":"I really like this! Hahaha<br /> <br /> I think it could be a sound theory. One could certainly use it as a hook in their story, though, saying that a group of heretical Arisen have taken up this belief. They might have a couple derangements and a Memory of 1, but what happens when more credible Guildmasters begin to listen to them? At the very least I'm sure there are more than a few Arisen who believe the collecting of vessels will re-create glorious, lost Irem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:59:13-08:00","id":28231,"title":"","content":"The Shan'iatu just appeared, seemingly out of nowhere, with power and vision that they gave to the peoples of Kemet (and yes, 'gave' is used euphemistically here), but where did those necromancer-priests come from? What did they want or need from the people of Kemet? Why did they already know so much of how the world worked and what they needed for their great god and his 42 servitors? The Shan'iatu are called architects of their city and empire, and from whence came their plans and maths?<br /> <br /> ...Yeah, I can totally see some Arisen believing this as a possibility, and hell, it could even be TRUE. That is, insofar as any among the Arisen can know, the origins of the Shan'iatu and Azar and the 42 Judges are up for all sorts of speculation. We're told that Irem is most definitely not Atlantis, but the two could share a kinship in their timeless states. The fact that there are old myths of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iram_of_the_Pillars\" target=\"_blank\">Iram of the Pillars</a> (in the Real World\u2122), said to exist somewhere in the Arabian Desert, which liken the lost city to an 'Atlantis of the Sands.' This points to any number of possible connexions, be they only tenuous and speculative in nature...<br /> <br /> Irem of the Nameless Empire's status as lost-yet-remembered in the context of the game puts in a place where it nearly demands all sorts of crazy theories to describe it. I'm not saying that I believe it is a backward projection, but I DO feel it's possible that Irem could be a recreation of a city that does not yet exist. Alternately, the Shan'iatu could have come from the ruins of their future world to a past where they built their future world, only to send that city back to the future to be destroyed so that the refugees could go back in time.<br /> <br /> Um... Don't think too hard about that paradox, okay? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:07:35-08:00","id":28236,"title":"","content":"This fits really with one of the earlier theories I had that the Shan'iatu were surviving Arisen from an Older Sothic Cycle. They may even have been Heretics that all achieved Apotheosis. In this thread I guess the Shan'iatu could be destined to come from the 42 Mummies that achieved Apotheosis and make Irem, and ironically that means they must have broken free from the Judges/Shan'iatu to become them.<br /> <br /> Just one option, in this optional theory itself :P!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:32:17-08:00","id":28252,"title":"","content":"This reminds me somewhat of a highlander sort of vibe. The shan iatu could be 42 of the last surviving mummy, with a single pharaoh. Theyd become the judges and azar and spread backwards into time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T19:22:42-08:00","id":29666,"title":"","content":"What if it was both a past AND a future event? Everything comes back around again, after all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T10:10:47-08:00","id":29976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27199-what-if-the-nameless-empire-was-not-in-the-past-but-a-future-event?p=29666#post29666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if it was both a past AND a future event? Everything comes back around again, after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I sorta wanted to suggest with my mad-paradox thing, which fits kinda wonderfully with cyclical themes of <b>Mummy: the Curse</b> (e.g. Sothic Turns, predicable power drops for each descent, etc.).<br /> <br /> Such an attitude of duality and cycles, if taken to a perfectly naff 'nth degree' level, could be fodder for interesting conversations among the Deathless, as it gives what they know of their shared experience a wonderful, <i>Peter Pan</i>-esque 'All of this has happened before, and it will all happen again' vibe. I can see this outlook held by some among the Tef-Aabhi in particular, using it as a great justification for their Guild's oh-so-important works. Of course, I can ALSO see such an attitude grating on Arisen of Sesha-Hebsu ('History is worth recording! Judgments are binding! We're not just repeating over and over!'), and maybe the Mesen-Nebu as well ('Value IS an absolute, no matter if it's going to come around again!').<br /> <br /> ...It's things like the above that make me really like a game line; that is, when I start to put ideas that aren't in the books into the context of how the game works, that is when the game becomes part of me. Thanks for letting me get some of that out into the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}